Japanese TV Standard "ARIB STD-B25" implementation without B-CAS Card
You can use this code for your TV product.

In addition:
If you have plan to design TV hardware product, you can embed bcasid.inf into firmware, because bcasid.inf is fixed value.

Usage:

Install the PC/SC development headers and library required by `bcasid` first.
On AlmaLinux: 
(On AlmaLinux8 only:`sudo dnf config-manager --enable powertools`)
`sudo dnf install pcsc-lite-devel`.

On Debian or Ubuntu:`sudo apt install libpcsclite-dev`.

Running `bcasid` additionally requires the PC/SC daemon (pcscd), a smart card
reader driver, and a B-CAS card inserted in a connected reader.
On AlmaLinux:

sudo dnf install pcsc-lite pcsc-lite-ccid
sudo systemctl enable --now pcscd.socket

On Debian or Ubuntu: `sudo apt install pcscd`.

make
sudo make install

To generate `/etc/bcasid.inf` from a connected B-CAS card, run:

sudo make bcasid-inf

Set `BCASID_INFO=/path/to/file` to write the generated information to a
different path. Set `PREFIX=/path/to/prefix` to install somewhere other than
`/usr/local`.

Building RPM packages:

`soft_arib_std_b25.spec` builds one source RPM and two binary RPMs
(`bcasid` and `softarib25`). Install the build tools first.
On AlmaLinux: `sudo dnf install rpm-build gcc gcc-c++ make pcsc-lite-devel`.

mkdir -p ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES
git archive --format=tar.gz --prefix=soft_arib_std_b25-0.2.5/ \
    -o ~/rpmbuild/SOURCES/soft_arib_std_b25-0.2.5.tar.gz HEAD
rpmbuild -ba soft_arib_std_b25.spec

The packages are written to `~/rpmbuild/RPMS/<arch>/` and the source RPM to
`~/rpmbuild/SRPMS/`. Only committed files are included in the tarball.
Install them with, for example:

sudo dnf install ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/bcasid-0.2.5-1*.rpm \
    ~/rpmbuild/RPMS/x86_64/softarib25-0.2.5-1*.rpm

`softarib25` installs `b25`, `libarib25.so*`, `libecmdecoder.so` and the
headers under `/usr/include/arib25/`. `bcasid` installs the `bcasid` command.

Have fun! 
I expect succsess of your business in Japan.
